          "kwargs": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "I see that the investigation findings haven't been created yet. Based on the context_map.json, I have comprehensive information about the BlogMaster AI project. Let me create a detailed Angular migration plan in Italian based on this context.\n\n---\n\n# Piano di Migrazione da Next.js/React ad Angular v20 per BlogMaster AI\n\n## Sommario Esecutivo\n\n**BlogMaster AI** è una piattaforma di generazione e gestione di contenuti blog alimentata da AI, attualmente costruita con **Next.js 14, React, TypeScript e Tailwind CSS**. La migrazione ad **Angular v20** rappresenta una trasformazione architettonica complessa che richiede:\n\n1. **Separazione del backend**: Le API routes di Next.js devono essere estratte in un backend standalone (NestJS consigliato)\n2. **Riscrittura completa del frontend**: Tutti i componenti React devono essere convertiti in componenti Angular\n3. **Cambio di paradigma**: Da React hooks e state management a RxJS observables e servizi Angular\n\n**Stima complessiva**: 12-16 settimane di sviluppo per un team di 2-3 sviluppatori full-stack con esperienza in entrambi i framework.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Analisi dello Stato Attuale\n\n### 1.1 Stack Tecnologico Corrente\n\n| Categoria | Tecnologia Attuale | Ruolo |\n|-----------|-------------------|-------|\n| **Framework Frontend** | Next.js 14 (App Router) | SSR, routing, rendering |\n| **UI Library** | React 18 | Componenti UI |\n| **Linguaggio** | TypeScript | Type safety |\n| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS | Utility-first CSS |\n| **Componenti UI** | shadcn/ui | Libreria componenti |\n| **Form Management** | React Hook Form + Zod | Gestione form e validazione |\n| **State Management** | Zustand / React Query | Store globale e cache |\n| **Backend** | Next.js API Routes | Endpoint REST |\n| **AI Orchestration** | Langchain | Integrazione LLM |\n| **LLM** | OpenAI GPT-4o | Generazione contenuti |\n| **Database** | SQLite + Prisma ORM | Persistenza dati |\n| **Deployment** | Docker + docker-compose | Containerizzazione |\n\n### 1.2 Struttura dell'Applicazione\n\n```\nblogmaster-ai/\n├── src/\n│   ├── app/                    # Next.js App Router + API routes\n│   │   ├── api/               # Backend endpoints\n│   │   │   ├── generate/      # AI content generation\n│   │   │   ├── posts/         # CRUD posts\n│   │   │   └── health/        # Health check\n│   │   ├── layout.tsx         # Root layout\n│   │   └── page.tsx           # Homepage\n│   ├── components/            # React components\n│   │   ├── content/           # Content-related components\n│   │   ├── editor/            # Rich text editor\n│   │   ├── layout/            # Layout components\n│   │   └── ui/                # shadcn/ui components\n│   ├── services/              # Business logic\n│   │   └── ai-content-generator.ts\n│   ├── store/                 # Zustand store\n│   │   └── blog-store.ts\n│   ├── lib/                   # Utilities + Prisma client\n│   ├── types/                 # TypeScript types\n│   └── prisma/                # Database schema\n└── docker-compose.yml\n```\n\n### 1.3 Funzionalità Principali\n\n- ✅ **Generazione contenuti AI**: Integrazione con GPT-4o tramite Langchain\n- ✅ **Editor rich text**: Editor WYSIWYG per contenuti blog\n- ✅ **Gestione post**: CRUD completo per articoli blog\n- ✅ **Post programmati**: Scheduling per pubblicazione futura\n- ✅ **Dark mode**: Tema scuro personalizzabile\n- ✅ **Dashboard**: Visualizzazione e gestione contenuti\n- ✅ **SSR**: Server-side rendering con Next.js\n\n---\n\n## 2. Perché Questa Migrazione è Complessa\n\n### 2.1 Sfide Architetturali\n\n#### **A. Next.js API Routes → Backend Separato**\nNext.js combina frontend e backend nello stesso progetto. Angular è un framework **solo frontend**, quindi:\n- ❌ Non può ospitare API routes server-side\n- ✅ Richiede un backend separato (NestJS, Express, Fastify)\n- ⚠️ Necessita di configurazione CORS e autenticazione separata\n\n#### **B. React Hooks → Angular Lifecycle + RxJS**\nReact usa hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useCallback`), Angular usa:\n- Lifecycle hooks (`ngOnInit`, `ngOnDestroy`)\n- RxJS Observables per gestione asincrona\n- Dependency Injection per servizi\n\n**Esempio di conversione**:\n\n```typescript\n// REACT (attuale)\nconst [posts, setPosts] = useState<Post[]>([]);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  fetch('/api/posts')\n    .then(res => res.json())\n    .then(data => setPosts(data));\n}, []);\n\n// ANGULAR (target)\nposts$: Observable<Post[]>;\n\nngOnInit() {\n  this.posts$ = this.postService.getPosts();\n}\n```\n\n#### **C. Zustand/React Query → NgRx/Akita/Services**\nLo state management cambia completamente:\n- React: Zustand (semplice, basato su hooks)\n- Angular: NgRx (Redux pattern), Akita, o servizi con BehaviorSubject\n\n#### **D. shadcn/ui → Angular Material/PrimeNG**\nI componenti UI devono essere sostituiti:\n- shadcn/ui è specifico per React\n- Angular Material o PrimeNG sono le alternative principali\n\n#### **E. React Hook Form → Angular Reactive Forms**\nLa gestione form cambia paradigma:\n- React Hook Form: uncontrolled components\n- Angular Reactive Forms: FormGroup, FormControl, Validators\n\n---\n\n## 3. Strategia di Migrazione Raccomandata\n\n### 3.1 Approccio: Backend Separation + Angular Frontend\n\n**Raccomandazione**: Migrazione **Big Bang** con separazione backend/frontend.\n\n**Motivazione**:\n- ✅ Architettura più pulita e scalabile\n- ✅ Backend riutilizzabile per future app (mobile, desktop)\n- ✅ Deploy indipendente di frontend e backend\n- ✅ Team separati possono lavorare in parallelo\n- ❌ Richiede più tempo iniziale (ma migliore a lungo termine)\n\n### 3.2 Stack Tecnologico Target\n\n| Categoria | Tecnologia Target | Motivazione |\n|-----------|------------------|-------------|\n| **Frontend Framework** | Angular v20 | Requisito del progetto |\n| **Linguaggio** | TypeScript | Già in uso, compatibile |\n| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS | Mantenibile, già configurato |\n| **Componenti UI** | Angular Material v20 | Ufficiale, ben documentato |\n| **Form Management** | Reactive Forms | Nativo Angular, potente |\n| **State Management** | NgRx (o servizi + RxJS) | Standard per app complesse |\n| **HTTP Client** | HttpClient (Angular) | Nativo, basato su RxJS |\n| **Backend Framework** | NestJS | TypeScript, architettura simile ad Angular |\n| **API Style** | REST (+ GraphQL opzionale) | Compatibile con frontend |\n| **ORM** | Prisma | Già in uso, mantenerlo |\n| **Database** | SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (prod) | Upgrade consigliato per produzione |\n| **AI Integration** | Langchain | Mantenerlo nel backend |\n| **Deployment** | Docker + Kubernetes | Scalabile, production-ready |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Piano di Migrazione Dettagliato\n\n### Fase 1: Preparazione e Setup (Settimane 1-2)\n\n#### **1.1 Analisi e Documentazione**\n- [ ] Audit completo del codice esistente\n- [ ] Mappatura di tutti i componenti React → Angular\n- [ ] Documentazione delle API esistenti\n- [ ] Identificazione delle dipendenze critiche\n- [ ] Creazione di test di regressione\n\n#### **1.2 Setup Backend (NestJS)**\n```bash\n# Creare nuovo progetto NestJS\nnest new blogmaster-backend\ncd blogmaster-backend\n\n# Installare dipendenze\nnpm install @prisma/client prisma\nnpm install @nestjs/config @nestjs/swagger\nnpm install langchain openai\nnpm install class-validator class-transformer\n```\n\n**Struttura backend**:\n```\nblogmaster-backend/\n├── src/\n│   ├── modules/\n│   │   ├── posts/\n│   │   │   ├── posts.controller.ts\n│   │   │   ├── posts.service.ts\n│   │   │   ├── posts.module.ts\n│   │   │   └── dto/\n│   │   ├── ai-generation/\n│   │   │   ├── ai-generation.controller.ts\n│   │   │   ├── ai-generation.service.ts\n│   │   │   └── ai-generation.module.ts\n│   │   └── health/\n│   ├── prisma/\n│   │   └── prisma.service.ts\n│   ├── config/\n│   └── main.ts\n├── prisma/\n│   └── schema.prisma\n└── package.json\n```\n\n#### **1.3 Setup Frontend (Angular v20)**\n```bash\n# Creare nuovo progetto Angular\nng new blogmaster-angular --routing --style=scss\ncd blogmaster-angular\n\n# Installare dipendenze\nng add @angular/material\nnpm install @ngrx/store @ngrx/effects @ngrx/entity\nnpm install tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer\nnpx tailwindcss init\nnpm install @tiptap/core @tiptap/angular  # Rich text editor\n```\n\n**Struttura frontend**:\n```\nblogmaster-angular/\n├── src/\n│   ├── app/\n│   │   ├── core/\n│   │   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   ├── guards/\n│   │   │   ├── interceptors/\n│   │   │   └── models/\n│   │   ├── features/\n│   │   │   ├── dashboard/\n│   │   │   ├── content-generator/\n│   │   │   ├── editor/\n│   │   │   └── posts/\n│   │   ├── shared/\n│   │   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── directives/\n│   │   │   └── pipes/\n│   │   ├── store/\n│   │   │   ├── actions/\n│   │   │   ├── reducers/\n│   │   │   ├── effects/\n│   │   │   └── selectors/\n│   │   └── app.component.ts\n│   ├── assets/\n│   └── environments/\n└── angular.json\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fase 2: Migrazione Backend (Settimane 3-5)\n\n#### **2.1 Migrazione Database e Prisma**\n- [ ] Copiare `prisma/schema.prisma` nel backend NestJS\n- [ ] Creare `PrismaService` per NestJS\n- [ ] Testare connessione database\n\n**File**: `src/prisma/prisma.service.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { Injectable, OnModuleInit } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class PrismaService extends PrismaClient implements OnModuleInit {\n  async onModuleInit() {\n    await this.$connect();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### **2.2 Migrazione API Endpoints**\n\n**Mappatura API**:\n\n| Endpoint Attuale | Controller NestJS | Metodo | Priorità |\n|-----------------|-------------------|--------|----------|\n| `POST /api/generate` | `AiGenerationController.generate()` | POST | Alta |\n| `POST /api/generate/titles` | `AiGenerationController.generateTitles()` | POST | Alta |\n| `GET /api/posts` | `PostsController.findAll()` | GET | Alta |\n| `GET /api/posts/:id` | `PostsController.findOne()` | GET | Alta |\n| `POST /api/posts` | `PostsController.create()` | POST | Alta |\n| `PUT /api/posts/:id` | `PostsController.update()` | PUT | Media |\n| `DELETE /api/posts/:id` | `PostsController.delete()` | DELETE | Media |\n| `GET /api/health` | `HealthController.check()` | GET | Bassa |\n\n**Esempio migrazione endpoint**:\n\n```typescript\n// NEXT.JS API ROUTE (src/app/api/posts/route.ts)\nexport async function GET() {\n  const posts = await prisma.post.findMany();\n  return NextResponse.json(posts);\n}\n\n// NESTJS CONTROLLER (src/modules/posts/posts.controller.ts)\n@Controller('posts')\nexport class PostsController {\n  constructor(private readonly postsService: PostsService) {}\n\n  @Get()\n  async findAll(): Promise<Post[]> {\n    return this.postsService.findAll();\n  }\n}\n\n// NESTJS SERVICE (src/modules/posts/posts.service.ts)\n@Injectable()\nexport class PostsService {\n  constructor(private prisma: PrismaService) {}\n\n  async findAll(): Promise<Post[]> {\n    return this.prisma.post.findMany();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### **2.3 Migrazione Servizio AI**\n- [ ] Portare `ai-content-generator.ts` in NestJS\n- [ ] Configurare Langchain e OpenAI\n- [ ] Creare DTO per richieste/risposte\n- [ ] Implementare error handling\n\n**File**: `src/modules/ai-generation/ai-generation.service.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { ChatOpenAI } from 'langchain/chat_models/openai';\nimport { PromptTemplate } from 'langchain/prompts';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class AiGenerationService {\n  private model: ChatOpenAI;\n\n  constructor() {\n    this.model = new ChatOpenAI({\n      modelName: 'gpt-4o',\n      temperature: 0.7,\n    });\n  }\n\n  async generateContent(prompt: string): Promise<string> {\n    const template = PromptTemplate.fromTemplate(\n      'Generate blog content about: {topic}'\n    );\n    const formattedPrompt = await template.format({ topic: prompt });\n    const response = await this.model.call([{ role: 'user', content: formattedPrompt }]);\n    return response.content;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### **2.4 Configurazione CORS e Swagger**\n```typescript\n// main.ts\nimport { NestFactory } from '@nestjs/core';\nimport { SwaggerModule, DocumentBuilder } from '@nestjs/swagger';\n\nasync function bootstrap() {\n  const app = await NestFactory.create(AppModule);\n  \n  // CORS per Angular frontend\n  app.enableCors({\n    origin: 'http://localhost:4200',\n    credentials: true,\n  });\n\n  // Swagger documentation\n  const config = new DocumentBuilder()\n    .setTitle('BlogMaster API')\n    .setVersion('1.0')\n    .build();\n  const document = SwaggerModule.createDocument(app, config);\n  SwaggerModule.setup('api', app, document);\n\n  await app.listen(3000);\n}\nbootstrap();\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fase 3: Migrazione Frontend Core (Settimane 6-9)\n\n#### **3.1 Setup Servizi HTTP**\n\n**File**: `src/app/core/services/post.service.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { Injectable } from '@angular/core';\nimport { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\nimport { Observable } from 'rxjs';\nimport { Post } from '../models/post.model';\nimport { environment } from '../../../environments/environment';\n\n@Injectable({\n  providedIn: 'root'\n})\nexport class PostService {\n  private apiUrl = `${environment.apiUrl}/posts`;\n\n  constructor(private http: HttpClient) {}\n\n  getPosts(): Observable<Post[]> {\n    return this.http.get<Post[]>(this.apiUrl);\n  }\n\n  getPost(id: string): Observable<Post> {\n    return this.http.get<Post>(`${this.apiUrl}/${id}`);\n  }\n\n  createPost(post: Partial<Post>): Observable<Post> {\n    return this.http.post<Post>(this.apiUrl, post);\n  }\n\n  updatePost(id: string, post: Partial<Post>): Observable<Post> {\n    return this.http.put<Post>(`${this.apiUrl}/${id}`, post);\n  }\n\n  deletePost(id: string): Observable<void> {\n    return this.http.delete<void>(`${this.apiUrl}/${id}`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### **3.2 Setup State Management (NgRx)**\n\n**Actions** (`src/app/store/actions/post.actions.ts`):\n```typescript\nimport { createAction, props } from '@ngrx/store';\nimport { Post } from '../../core/models/post.model';\n\nexport const loadPosts = createAction('[Post] Load Posts');\nexport const loadPostsSuccess = createAction(\n  '[Post] Load Posts Success',\n  props<{ posts: Post[] }>()\n);\nexport const loadPostsFailure = createAction(\n  '[Post] Load Posts Failure',\n  props<{ error: any }>()\n);\n```\n\n**Reducer** (`src/app/store/reducers/post.reducer.ts`):\n```typescript\nimport { createReducer, on } from '@ngrx/store';\nimport * as PostActions from '../actions/post.actions';\nimport { Post } from '../../core/models/post.model';\n\nexport interface PostState {\n  posts: Post[];\n  loading: boolean;\n  error: any;\n}\n\nexport const initialState: PostState = {\n  posts: [],\n  loading: false,\n  error: null\n};\n\nexport const postReducer = createReducer(\n  initialState,\n  on(PostActions.loadPosts, state => ({ ...state, loading: true })),\n  on(PostActions.loadPostsSuccess, (state, { posts }) => ({\n    ...state,\n    posts,\n    loading: false\n  })),\n  on(PostActions.loadPostsFailure, (state, { error }) => ({\n    ...state,\n    error,\n    loading: false\n  }))\n);\n```\n\n**Effects** (`src/app/store/effects/post.effects.ts`):\n```typescript\nimport { Injectable } from '@angular/core';\nimport { Actions, createEffect, ofType } from '@ngrx/effects';\nimport { of } from 'rxjs';\nimport { map, catchError, switchMap } from 'rxjs/operators';\nimport * as PostActions from '../actions/post.actions';\nimport { PostService } from '../../core/services/post.service';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class PostEffects {\n  loadPosts$ = createEffect(() =>\n    this.actions$.pipe(\n      ofType(PostActions.loadPosts),\n      switchMap(() =>\n        this.postService.getPosts().pipe(\n          map(posts => PostActions.loadPostsSuccess({ posts })),\n          catchError(error => of(PostActions.loadPostsFailure({ error })))\n        )\n      )\n    )\n  );\n\n  constructor(\n    private actions$: Actions,\n    private postService: PostService\n  ) {}\n}\n```\n\n#### **3.3 Migrazione Componenti UI**\n\n**Mappatura Componenti**:\n\n| Componente React | Componente Angular | Complessità | Stima |\n|-----------------|-------------------|-------------|-------|\n| `content-generator.tsx` | `ContentGeneratorComponent` | Alta | 8h |\n| `rich-text-editor.tsx` | `RichTextEditorComponent` | Alta | 12h |\n| `dashboard.tsx` | `DashboardComponent` | Media | 6h |\n| `button.tsx` (shadcn) | `mat-button` (Material) | Bassa | 1h |\n| `card.tsx` | `mat-card` | Bassa | 1h |\n| `dialog.tsx` | `mat-dialog` | Media | 3h |\n| `form.tsx` | Reactive Forms | Media | 4h |\n| `input.tsx` | `mat-input` | Bassa | 1h |\n| `select.tsx` | `mat-select` | Bassa | 1h |\n| `textarea.tsx` | `mat-input` (multiline) | Bassa | 1h |\n\n**Esempio migrazione componente**:\n\n```typescript\n// REACT (content-generator.tsx)\nexport function ContentGenerator() {\n  const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState('');\n  const [content, setContent] = useState('');\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);\n\n  const handleGenerate = async () => {\n    setLoading(true);\n    const response = await fetch('/api/generate', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify({ prompt }),\n    });\n    const data = await response.json();\n    setContent(data.content);\n    setLoading(false);\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input value={prompt} onChange={(e) => setPrompt(e.target.value)} />\n      <button onClick={handleGenerate} disabled={loading}>\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      <div>{content}</div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\n// ANGULAR (content-generator.component.ts)\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-content-generator',\n  templateUrl: './content-generator.component.html',\n  styleUrls: ['./content-generator.component.scss']\n})\nexport class ContentGeneratorComponent {\n  promptControl = new FormControl('');\n  content$ = new BehaviorSubject<string>('');\n  loading$ = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(false);\n\n  constructor(private aiService: AiGenerationService) {}\n\n  handleGenerate(): void {\n    const prompt = this.promptControl.value;\n    if (!prompt) return;\n\n    this.loading$.next(true);\n    this.aiService.generateContent(prompt)\n      .pipe(\n        finalize(() => this.loading$.next(false))\n      )\n      .subscribe({\n        next: (content) => this.content$.next(content),\n        error: (error) => console.error(error)\n      });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<!-- content-generator.component.html -->\n<div class=\"content-generator\">\n  <mat-form-field appearance=\"outline\">\n    <mat-label>Prompt</mat-label>\n    <input matInput [formControl]=\"promptControl\" />\n  </mat-form-field>\n\n  <button \n    mat-raised-button \n    color=\"primary\"\n    (click)=\"handleGenerate()\"\n    [disabled]=\"loading$ | async\">\n    <mat-spinner *ngIf=\"loading$ | async\" diameter=\"20\"></mat-spinner>\n    Generate\n  </button>\n\n  <div class=\"content-output\">\n    {{ content$ | async }}\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n#### **3.4 Migrazione Rich Text Editor**\n\nPer l'editor rich text, usare **Tiptap Angular**:\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tiptap/core @tiptap/pm @tiptap/starter-kit\nnpm install @tiptap/angular\n```\n\n```typescript\n// rich-text-editor.component.ts\nimport { Component, OnInit, OnDestroy } from '@angular/core';\nimport { Editor } from '@tiptap/core';\nimport StarterKit from '@tiptap/starter-kit';\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-rich-text-editor',\n  templateUrl: './rich-text-editor.component.html',\n  styleUrls: ['./rich-text-editor.component.scss']\n})\nexport class RichTextEditorComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy {\n  editor: Editor;\n\n  ngOnInit(): void {\n    this.editor = new Editor({\n      extensions: [StarterKit],\n      content: '<p>Start writing...</p>',\n    });\n  }\n\n  ngOnDestroy(): void {\n    this.editor.destroy();\n  }\n\n  getContent(): string {\n    return this.editor.getHTML();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fase 4: Funzionalità Avanzate (Settimane 10-12)\n\n#### **4.1 Routing e Lazy Loading**\n\n```typescript\n// app-routing.module.ts\nconst routes: Routes = [\n  {\n    path: '',\n    component: DashboardComponent\n  },\n  {\n    path: 'posts',\n    loadChildren: () => import('./features/posts/posts.module')\n      .then(m => m.PostsModule)\n  },\n  {\n    path: 'generate',\n    loadChildren: () => import('./features/content-generator/content-generator.module')\n      .then(m => m.ContentGeneratorModule)\n  },\n  {\n    path: 'editor/:id',\n    loadChildren: () => import('./features/editor/editor.module')\n      .then(m => m.EditorModule)\n  }\n];\n```\n\n#### **4.2 Dark Mode**\n\n```typescript\n// theme.service.ts\n@Injectable({\n  providedIn: 'root'\n})\nexport class ThemeService {\n  private darkMode$ = new BehaviorSubject<boolean>(false);\n\n  constructor() {\n    const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('theme');\n    this.darkMode$.next(savedTheme === 'dark');\n  }\n\n  toggleDarkMode(): void {\n    const newValue = !this.darkMode$.value;\n    this.darkMode$.next(newValue);\n    localStorage.setItem('theme', newValue ? 'dark' : 'light');\n    this.applyTheme(newValue);\n  }\n\n  private applyTheme(isDark: boolean): void {\n    if (isDark) {\n      document.body.classList.add('dark-theme');\n    } else {\n      document.body.classList.remove('dark-theme');\n    }\n  }\n\n  isDarkMode(): Observable<boolean> {\n    return this.darkMode$.asObservable();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### **4.3 Post Programmati**\n\n```typescript\n// scheduled-posts.service.ts\n@Injectable({\n  providedIn: 'root'\n})\nexport class ScheduledPostsService {\n  constructor(\n    private http: HttpClient,\n    private postService: PostService\n  ) {}\n\n  schedulePost(post: Partial<Post>, publishDate: Date): Observable<Post> {\n    return this.http.post<Post>(`${environment.apiUrl}/posts/schedule`, {\n      ...post,\n      scheduledFor: publishDate.toISOString(),\n      status: 'scheduled'\n    });\n  }\n\n  getScheduledPosts(): Observable<Post[]> {\n    return this.http.get<Post[]>(`${environment.apiUrl}/posts?status=scheduled`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Fase 5: Testing e QA (Settimane 13-14)\n\n#### **5.1 Unit Testing**\n\n```typescript\n// post.service.spec.ts\ndescribe('PostService', () => {\n  let service: PostService;\n  let httpMock: HttpTestingController;\n\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    TestBed.configureTestingModule({\n      imports: [HttpClientTestingModule],\n      providers: [PostService]\n    });\n    service = TestBed.inject(PostService);\n    httpMock = TestBed.inject(HttpTestingController);\n  });\n\n  it('should fetch posts', () => {\n    const mockPosts: Post[] = [\n      { id: '1', title: 'Test', content: 'Content' }\n    ];\n\n    service.getPosts().subscribe(posts => {\n      expect(posts).toEqual(mockPosts);\n    });\n\n    const req = httpMock.expectOne(`${environment.apiUrl}/posts`);\n    expect(req.request.method).toBe('GET');\n    req.flush(mockPosts);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n#### **5.2 E2E Testing (Cypress)**\n\n```bash\nnpm install --save-dev cypress\nnpx cypress open\n```\n\n```typescript\n// cypress/e2e/content-generation.cy.ts\ndescribe('Content Generation', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    cy.visit('/generate');\n  });\n\n  it('should generate content from prompt', () => {\n    cy.get('[data-testid=\"prompt-input\"]')\n      .type('Write about Angular migration');\n    \n    cy.get('[data-testid=\"generate-button\"]').click();\n    \n    cy.get('[data-testid=\"content-output\"]', { timeout: 10000 })\n      .should('not.be.empty');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n#### **5.3 Checklist Testing**\n\n- [ ] Unit test per tutti i servizi (coverage > 80%)\n- [ ] Unit test per componenti critici\n- [ ] E2E test per flussi principali\n- [ ] Test di integrazione backend\n- [ ] Test di performance (Lighthouse score > 90)\n- [ ] Test di accessibilità (WCAG 2.1 AA)\n- [ ] Test cross-browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\n- [ ] Test responsive (mobile, tablet, desktop)\n\n---\n\n### Fase 6: Deployment e Go-Live (Settimane 15-16)\n\n#### **6.1 Configurazione Docker**\n\n**Backend Dockerfile**:\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:20-alpine\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package*.json ./\nRUN npm ci --only=production\nCOPY . .\nRUN npx prisma generate\nRUN npm run build\nEXPOSE 3000\nCMD [\"node\", \"dist/main\"]\n```\n\n**Frontend Dockerfile**:\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:20-alpine AS builder\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY package*.json ./\nRUN npm ci\nCOPY . .\nRUN npm run build -- --configuration production\n\nFROM nginx:alpine\nCOPY --from=builder /app/dist/blogmaster-angular /usr/share/nginx/html\nCOPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\nEXPOSE 80\nCMD [\"nginx\", \"-g\", \"daemon off;\"]\n```\n\n**docker-compose.yml**:\n```yaml\nversion: '3.8'\n\nservices:\n  backend:\n    build: ./blogmaster-backend\n    ports:\n      - \"3000:3000\"\n    environment:\n      - DATABASE_URL=file:./dev.db\n      - OPENAI_API_KEY=${OPENAI_API_KEY}\n    volumes:\n      - ./data:/app/data\n\n  frontend:\n    build: ./blogmaster-angular\n    ports:\n      - \"80:80\"\n    depends_on:\n      - backend\n    environment:\n      - API_URL=http://backend:3000\n```\n\n#### **6.2 CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)**\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/deploy.yml\nname: Deploy BlogMaster\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3\n        with:\n          node-version: '20'\n      \n      - name: Test Backend\n        run: |\n          cd blogmaster-backend\n          npm ci\n          npm run test\n      \n      - name: Test Frontend\n        run: |\n          cd blogmaster-angular\n          npm ci\n          npm run test:ci\n\n  deploy:\n    needs: test\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - name: Deploy to production\n        run: |\n          docker-",
